DRONE SURVEILLANCE MODERNIZATION

Omnitechnical Architecture • Sandbox • Read-Only Governance • IV Pillars • Foundation to Clocker

Your proposed architecture introduces a surveillance-information governance layer into the broader EC64.44 and Xenograph Analytics environment.

The central concept is to transform drone-acquired information into classified, geographically referenced, cryptographically accountable, and auditable evidence, without allowing the acquisition system to exercise unrestricted authority over the information or the people represented in it.

I would organize the proposal around four foundations:

1. Sandbox: Isolated execution and experimentation.
2. Read-Only: Observation without unauthorized modification.
3. IV Pillars: Four independent governance and verification responsibilities.
4. Foundation to Clocker: A traceable progression from raw acquisition to synchronized temporal and analytical records.

The following is a proposed technical blueprint, preserving your terminology while distinguishing established engineering mechanisms from conceptual designations.


