III. RBGY Coded Nexus

Your RGBY arrangement establishes a four-part geographic classification.

Code	Color	Assigned network	Proposed designation

R	Red	North America	Northern American network
G	Green	West America	Western American network
B	Blue	East Asia	Eastern Asian network
Y	Yellow	South Asia	Southern Asian network


Technical distinction: These are custom organizational assignments, not established geographic or telecommunications standards.

There is also an overlap to resolve: North America and West America are not mutually exclusive geographical regions. A geographic registry should therefore specify exact boundaries, jurisdiction codes, and coordinate reference systems.

For actual mapping, use recognized geospatial standards such as WGS 84 coordinates, GeoJSON, and standardized country or regional identifiers.

Systemic color articulation

