X. Foundation to Clocker

This is the most important integration point with EC64.44.

The Foundation represents the trusted starting conditions. The Clocker represents the synchronized temporal and operational reference environment.

Stage	Name	Responsibility

01	Foundation	Initial system configuration
02	Acquisition	Capture authorized information
03	Identification	Establish source and account identity
04	Classification	Assign data categories
05	Indexing	Register searchable references
06	Verification	Validate authenticity and integrity
07	Temporal alignment	Connect records to EC64.44
08	Clocker	Maintain synchronized temporal state
09	Analytics	Evaluate relationships and patterns
10	Auditorium	Present supporting evidence
11	Preservation	Archive verified records


Drone record and EC64.44 alignment

Every authorized acquisition should preserve two time references:

1. Original Earth-time timestamp.
2. Derived EC64.44 timestamp.

The original timestamp should never be overwritten by the converted value.

A conversion record should preserve the time-zone reference, synchronization source, conversion algorithm version, and any uncertainty.

This is particularly important when correlating imagery with environmental sensors or other independently recorded events.


